# Below are some examples of some very useful Maple command which 
# can be used to solve Problems 1, 3, and 4 on HW#2: 
# 

 2^51203; # this one should immediately yield the full decimal 
          # expansion of 2^51203 

 seq(2^k mod 11,k=1..100); # this yields all the powers 2^1, 2^2, ..., 2^100 
                           # mod 11. 

 with(numtheory); # this calls in Maple's number theory library, 
                  # to enable useful commands like order. 
 order(2,101); # this command tells you the order of 2 mod 101. 

 Power(3,2^2048+1) mod 11; # note that 3^(2^2048+1) mod 11 yields an error, 
                          # because maple uses the naive algorithm (unless 
                          # told to do otherwise) and maple realizes that 
                          # the naive algorithm will take too long. The 
                          # Power command tells Maple to use the binary 
                          # method, and thus allows much larger powers... 


